# --- The Intermediate -> Merged generator ---
# CORRECTED 2026-08-02 (audit): an earlier note here called LinearizeMerged.v a "fake
# lin_side linearizer (confused-session detour)".  That was WRONG.  Its [compiler_gen] is
#     Merged.transitional_to_merged_gen make upd (prog_buffers pr)
#                                       (Transitional.intermediate_to_transitional pr)
# i.e. the REAL pipeline, composed from the two main-line definitions; it differs from
# [Merged.transitional_to_merged] only in taking LabelScheme.v's canonical (collision-free,
# separately-compilable) label numbering instead of the legacy one.  This file proves the
# generator's STATIC well-formedness only -- there is no semantic simulation here.
# What WAS abandoned is the Lin*.v SIMULATION (an Intermediate->Merged proof that had to
# reconcile Intermediate's gps return stack with the backend's R_RA discipline), archived
# 2026-07-20 to Recomposition/OldUnused/Lin*.v together with its RSC instantiation
# (MicroPolicies/OldUnused/K*.v).  An abandoned PROOF, not a fake COMPILER.
# The S2T/ development supersedes that attempt: T is already the R_RA machine, so a
# T -> Merged simulation has no gps/R_RA reconciliation to do.
# RSC_MD_MP.v (the functor) is independent of all of this.
